 "text": "Ag-Land FS | Ag-Land FS Your Privacy Choices\nWe and our vendors use technology that collects data about your use of our site so we can improve and personalize our products and services, for analytics and marketing, and to fulfill your requests. We may also share this information with marketing vendors, social media companies, and analytics partners. By using our website, you acknowledge and agree to our Terms of Use. To learn more about our privacy practices review our Privacy Policy . P lease review your choices.\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nSkip to Main Content FS Cooperatives\nCareers\nOur Locations\nContact Us\nCredit Application\nCash Bids\nmyFS Login\nAgriculture Agronomy\nAdjuvants\nCorn\nCorn Silage\nPlant Performance\nSoybeans\nWheat\nForages\nCrop Protection\nCrop Nutrients\nFS Agri-Finance\nEnergy\nPropane\nFuels & Additives\nLubricants\nEnergy Equipment\nGrain\nCash Bids\nFutures\nDTN Options\nGrain Marketing\nGrain Systems & Buildings\nFS Agri-Finance\nFunded by Farmers for Farmers\nReview our flexible financing offers.\nCommercial Energy\nPropane\nFuels & Additives\nLubricants\nEnergy Equipment\nFAST STOP Gas Stations\nTurf\nTurf Seeds\nTurf Management\nLubricants\nProtect Your Assets\nWe deliver ultimate performance and protection, on-road or off-road. \nResidential Energy\nPropane\nFAST STOP Gas Stations\nTurf\nTurf Seeds\nTurf Management\nPropane\nWe Bring the Heat\nReliable propane supply to power your home.\nNews and Resources News\nmyFS Solution Center\nCredit Application\nAbout Us About Us\nCareers\nContact Us\nShowing slide 1 of 5 slides\nFs agronomy\nMaximize profitability.\nLearn More\nmyfs solution center\nThe digital enhancement to your personalized relationship with FS.\nLearn More\nCareers\nExplore our current openings and apply today!\nSearch Jobs\nYour heat, your home, your way.\nWhen it comes to your home, you want dependable service, the most reliable propane supply and programs that fit your needs. Ag-Land FS delivers.\nLearn More\nNEW FAST STOP Cardholders SAVE for 90 DAYS!\nLearn More\nCommitted to your success from start to finish\nWe deliver exceptional products and services tailored to you. Serving Logan, Peoria, and Tazewell counties.\nCorn\nElite genetics to deliver performance on your farm\nsoybeans\nFlexible, high-yield varieties for every platform\nPropane\nReliable supply for farms, homes, and businesses\nFuels\nQuality fuels and additives to keep your operation running\nLubricants\nPremium lubricants for ultimate protection\nTurf\nThe product in the industry\nWho We are\nThe FS brand represents a standard of excellence for agricultural and energy-related products. It's the people who represent the FS brand that set it apart. Always professional and dependable, FS specialists are trusted advisors who understand local needs.\nAbout Ag-Land FS\n100+\nOver 100 years focused on providing exceptional service and expertise\n20+\nLocations conveniently serving farmers and businesses across Logan, Peoria, and Tazewell counties in West Central Illinois\nMyfs solution center\nManage your account anytime, anywhere, and on any device with the myFS Solution Center. Whether you need to review past transactions, make payments, or manage your services, myFS Solution Center puts everything at your fingertips—streamlining your experience so you can focus on what matters most.\nMake secure online payments\nTrack order history and transactions\nManage services and deliveries\nLearn More\nStay Informed\nExpert Tips and Local News to Keep You Growing\nView All Articles\nShowing slides 1-3 of 3 slides\nPost-Harvest Equipment Maintenance: Tips to Avoid Downtime Next Season\nDuring post-harvest, putting your equipment away is not the end of the maintenance cycle. Post-harvest starts next season's reliability plan.\nSoybeans\nSoybean Harvest Considerations\nAs wet weather conditions continue, multiple wetting and drying cycles beyond maturity results in soybean pod sutures breaking open and the seed falling to the soil surface. These soybeans are unable to be harvested and could be a reason for lower-than-expected yields.\nAgronomy Services\nFall Nitrogen Application\nProper soil temperature combined with a forecast of downward-trending, assures you of the best chance of preserving your fall-applied anhydrous ammonia. Read about other useful practices that will help keep N available for next spring's crop.\nFind your Local Ag-Land FS\nZip Code\nSearch\nPekin\n1505 Valle Vista\nPekin , IL 61554\n(309) 346-4145\nAgriculture\nCommercial\nResidential\nNews & Resources\nAbout Us\nCareers\nPay My Bill\nmyFS Agronomy\nEmployees\nCredit\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\n© Copyright 2026 GROWMARK, Inc.\nAg-Land FS | Ag-Land FS",
